From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denchiklut <ollylut@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:25:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] oa: ask the page to undo before the window, as ArcCore does

RenderWidgetHostViewCocoa's undo: and redo: send the command to the focused frame with a reply, ExecuteEditCommandWithResult on the view's host and on the frame's input handler, which says whether the frame ran it. When it did not, the first undo manager up the responder chain that can undo or redo does, which is the window's: a page's own typing is undone first, and a press the page has no use for undoes what the app registered. ArcCore's view does the same through a method it adds before ExecuteEditCommand on both interfaces.
---
